This is impossible in several ways: Polymorph traps can only be generated
deeper in the dungeon, never on DL1. Polymorph traps don't disappear when a
monster steps on them (only when you do). And, as you correctly noted, your
pet would have stayed tame.

What you should have done is read through all the game messages by
(repeatedly) pressing Ctrl-P to see if you missed a "sad feeling". It is
still possible that your pet hit a trap door while you were in another
room, but in that case you'll find it on one of the next levels. Bring
something to eat.

